// == TRACK 4 - LAYER 3 - THREAT (boss tier only) =============================
// LIGHTCYCLE's top layer, REWRITTEN as a TRANCE GATE. The old lead was a
// stepwise call-and-response line — the same melodic shape Neon and Outrun
// already use for their leads, so the boss tier of the racing track sounded
// like the other two songs wearing a different hat. What replaced it shares
// nothing with them: rhythmic GATED CHORDS, the defining trance gesture, and
// no other layer in the whole soundtrack is chordal-rhythmic.
//
// The payload is unchanged: this is still the only layer that states the mode.
// Bars 3-4 gate a full Bb-major triad over the bass's bb pedal — the Phrygian
// bII as a CHORD, hammered in sixteenths, which is far more menacing than the
// old single bb5 passing note. Bar 7 states Gm, bar 8 F, so the descent home
// is fully harmonised for the first time.
//
// struct() carries the gate: one 16-step on/off cell per bar over slowcat'd
// chords. Bar 4 gates one extra hit (a push into the A half), bar 8 gates
// three fewer — the seam bar has to end in rests (see below).
setcps(0.5)
stack(
  note(`<[a4,c5,e5] [a4,c5,e5] [bb4,d5,f5] [bb4,d5,f5]
         [a4,c5,e5] [a4,c5,e5] [g4,bb4,d5] [f4,a4,c5]>`)
    .struct(`<[t ~ t t ~ t t ~ t ~ t t ~ t ~ ~]
              [t ~ t t ~ t t ~ t ~ t t ~ t ~ ~]
              [t ~ t t ~ t t ~ t ~ t t ~ t ~ ~]
              [t ~ t t ~ t t ~ t ~ t t ~ t t ~]
              [t ~ t t ~ t t ~ t ~ t t ~ t ~ ~]
              [t ~ t t ~ t t ~ t ~ t t ~ t ~ ~]
              [t ~ t t ~ t t ~ t ~ t t ~ t ~ ~]
              [t ~ t t ~ t t ~ t ~ t ~ ~ ~ ~ ~]>`)
    // WRAP SEAM. The build measures the discontinuity where the loop meets
    // itself; a bar 8 still sounding at the cut leaves a loud last sample
    // against a near-zero first one — an audible click every 16s. Ending bar 8
    // on RESTS (the gate's last three steps) leaves the seam carrying only
    // ring-out on both sides, and the tail-fold bridges it. The reverb and
    // delay are load-bearing for that bridge — do not trim them.
    .s("supersaw").unison(5).detune(0.18).spread(0.5)
    .hpf(280)                       // stays out of the bass and stab bands
    .lpf(3600).lpq(4)
    .attack(0.004).release(0.07)
    .gain(0.045)                    // set by meter: unison sums voices raw
    .delay(0.30).delaytime(0.375).delayfeedback(0.28)
    .room(0.25).size(0.7),

  // Sub-octave stab on the bar root, 8ths not 16ths. Half the rate of the
  // layer 0 engine, so it reads as a heavier machine pulling alongside rather
  // than as the same engine louder. Filtered hard to stay clear of the bass.
  note("<[a2*8] [a2*8] [bb2*8] [bb2*8] [a2*8] [a2*8] [g2*8] [f2*8]>")
    .s("square").lpf(420).gain(0.085).release(0.03)
)
